<section class="full" aria-label="Case study">
  <div class="card">

    <div class="callout">
      40–50 inconsistent source tags consolidated. 60+ interviewers enabled in two months. Reliable reporting infrastructure built without replicating legacy system debt.
    </div>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="Context">
      <h2 class="section-title">Context</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        During a global migration to Greenhouse, 4–6 regional SMEs were appointed to configure
        and implement the system locally. I served as the U.S. regional SME, responsible for
        system configuration, workflow design, template setup, automation sequencing,
        and training and adoption support.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        The rollout window was two months.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="The constraint">
      <h2 class="section-title">The Constraint</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The legacy ATS contained deeply inconsistent data and workflows. The risk was not migration failure —
        the risk was institutionalizing inconsistency inside a new system.
      </p>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>40–50 overlapping source tags with no structured taxonomy</li>
        <li>Inconsistent manual data entry across recruiters</li>
        <li>Fragmented candidate communication with no standard sequencing</li>
        <li>Variable interview scorecards by role and manager</li>
        <li>Unreliable reporting outputs from the legacy system</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="What we did">
      <h2 class="section-title">What We Did</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        I approached the migration as infrastructure design, not just system replacement.
      </p>

      <h3>Structured Taxonomy Design</h3>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Audited and consolidated legacy source tags into structured categories and subcategories</li>
        <li>Advocated for automatic source capture wherever Greenhouse supported it</li>
        <li>Referenced documentation directly when central implementation leads underestimated configuration capabilities — ensuring automation was maximized rather than manual processes recreated</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Evaluation Framework Standardization</h3>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Redesigned interview scorecards for clarity and consistency</li>
        <li>Standardized evaluation criteria across roles and hiring managers</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Automation & Workflow Sequencing</h3>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Built tokenized email templates for consistent candidate communications</li>
        <li>Configured stage-based automation triggers</li>
        <li>Reduced manual intake steps between approval and requisition creation</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Adoption & Enablement</h3>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Trained and supported 60+ interviewers during the regional rollout</li>
        <li>Monitored usage discipline and reinforced structured data entry practices</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="Impact">
      <h2 class="section-title">Impact</h2>
      <ul class="muted">
        <li>Reduced manual data correction and downstream reporting cleanup</li>
        <li>Created structured, reportable source tracking from day one</li>
        <li>Standardized evaluation processes across teams</li>
        <li>Automated candidate communications for consistency at scale</li>
        <li>Increased trust in reporting outputs and forecasting inputs</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout">
        The system became scalable rather than personality-dependent.
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="rule"></div>

    <section aria-label="Why it matters">
      <h2 class="section-title">Why It Matters</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Hiring infrastructure determines whether talent operations are predictable or reactive.
        Migration is not just a technical exercise — it is a governance decision.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Clean configuration, disciplined taxonomy, and automation reduce downstream friction
        and make forecasting, reporting, and planning reliable. Infrastructure design compounds over time.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</section>
